{%- comment -%}
  Judge.me rating summary for a product card, e.g. "★★★★☆ (96)".

  Emits bare text into whichever element the caller supplies so the card's
  existing rating styling applies unchanged. The numbers come from the Shopify
  product-rating metafields that the Judge.me app syncs on every review change,
  so no request is made at render time.

  Products with no reviews yet fall back to the caller's copy rather than
  printing "☆☆☆☆☆ (0)", which would read as a bad rating.

  Accepts:
  - product  {Object} product to show the rating for
  - fallback {String} optional copy for products without reviews, or for
    product-grid cards that are configured without a linked product

  Usage:
  {% render 'judgeme-rating-summary', product: product, fallback: block.settings.rating %}
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign jm_rating = product.metafields.reviews.rating.value.rating
  assign jm_count = product.metafields.reviews.rating_count.value | plus: 0
-%}
{%- if product != blank and jm_count > 0 -%}
  {%- render 'judgeme-stars', rating: jm_rating %} ({{ jm_count }})
{%- elsif fallback != blank -%}
  {{ fallback | escape }}
{%- endif -%}
